WEBVTT

00:01.168 --> 00:04.439
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.567 --> 00:07.871
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.923 --> 00:11.344
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.395 --> 00:14.318
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.385 --> 00:17.905
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.974 --> 00:21.128
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.196 --> 00:22.730
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.781 --> 00:24.167
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.234 --> 00:27.042
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.134 --> 00:35.670
So, Cleveland,
you got to be pretty psyched

00:35.736 --> 00:37.105
about President Ubama, huh?

00:37.173 --> 00:38.624
W-What?

00:38.691 --> 00:40.711
Well, I mean, you remember how
a lot of people said, like,

00:40.795 --> 00:42.330
"Oh, Ubama's not gonna
be able to do it,"

00:42.398 --> 00:43.566
but he's-he's
hanging in there.

00:43.634 --> 00:45.252
Peter, it's "Obama."

00:45.320 --> 00:47.221
Eh, You-bama, Me-bama,
We-bama, who cares?

00:47.289 --> 00:49.509
It's a black guy in a suit,
let's just marvel at that.

00:49.577 --> 00:50.978
Gosh, Cleveland,
it sure is great

00:51.046 --> 00:53.532
having you back at The Clam,
even if it's just for a week.

00:53.599 --> 00:55.519
(ringtone):
♪ My name is Cleveland Brown ♪

00:55.587 --> 00:57.455
♪ And I am proud to be... ♪

00:57.523 --> 00:59.158
Oh, hang on, that's
my cell phone.

00:59.226 --> 01:00.994
Aw, Peter,
you're using the song!

01:01.062 --> 01:02.264
Thank you.

01:02.331 --> 01:03.666
Well, the numbers
ain't so good,

01:03.733 --> 01:05.586
so we got to do everything
we can-- Hello, Lois.

01:05.654 --> 01:07.139
Peter, where the hell are you?

01:07.206 --> 01:09.525
You told me you were gonna clean
out those boxes in the basement

01:09.593 --> 01:10.728
and put them in the attic.

01:10.795 --> 01:12.180
Lois, it just sounds like
busy work.

01:12.248 --> 01:13.599
It is busy work.

01:13.667 --> 01:15.603
I'm trying to keep you
off the streets and off drugs.

01:15.671 --> 01:17.674
I'm selling those candy bars!

01:19.810 --> 01:22.648
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey, you
want to buy some candy bars

01:22.716 --> 01:25.020
so we can get some new uniforms
for our baseball team?

01:25.087 --> 01:26.939
Where'd you get
those candy bars?

01:28.075 --> 01:29.626
Peter, I need you home.

01:29.694 --> 01:31.797
You also promised you'd fix
that shelf in the garage.

01:31.865 --> 01:32.998
Oh, Lois, I'm losing you.

01:33.066 --> 01:34.584
(makes static noises)

01:34.635 --> 01:36.471
Hello? Hello?

01:36.539 --> 01:37.473
Hello?

01:37.558 --> 01:38.726
Oh, hey, Lois.

01:38.793 --> 01:40.427
This is somebody else now.

01:40.496 --> 01:42.331
There must've been
a cross connection.

01:42.399 --> 01:44.468
My name is Mike,
and I'm somewhere else

01:44.535 --> 01:45.737
trying to make my own call.

01:45.804 --> 01:47.138
Fine, Mike.

01:47.207 --> 01:49.275
You tell Peter he's in trouble
when he gets home.

01:49.343 --> 01:52.047
You can tell him yourself,
because Mike is Peter!

01:52.115 --> 01:53.182
Oh, my God.

01:53.250 --> 01:54.418
Are you serious?

01:54.486 --> 01:55.987
That was very good, Peter.

01:56.055 --> 01:57.089
I know!

01:57.158 --> 01:58.525
(sighs)
Geez.

01:58.593 --> 02:00.711
That's all my life is lately,
just a bunch of chores.

02:00.778 --> 02:03.248
I'm sick of Lois always
making me do stupid stuff.

02:03.317 --> 02:04.618
I know what you're saying,
Peter.

02:04.686 --> 02:05.988
Bonnie's always making me do

02:06.055 --> 02:08.392
all these impossible
household tasks.

02:08.460 --> 02:09.927
BONNIE:
Joe, make sure you get

02:09.994 --> 02:12.298
all the tire tracks
out of the carpet.

02:23.468 --> 02:24.969
Learn to live with it, Bonnie!

02:25.037 --> 02:26.172
There are tracks!

02:26.239 --> 02:27.706
People make tracks!

02:27.774 --> 02:28.910
Boy, I hear you, too.

02:28.977 --> 02:30.411
It's a lot of work
just to keep

02:30.479 --> 02:32.148
my single guy fridge
sufficiently depressing.

02:33.585 --> 02:34.652
Let's see.

02:34.719 --> 02:36.254
Ex-girlfriend's Yoplait.

02:36.322 --> 02:37.825
Root beer from two Julys ago.

02:37.892 --> 02:39.494
Here we go, expired milk.

02:39.562 --> 02:41.596
(chuckles)

02:41.664 --> 02:44.034
Oh, my God, Jenny,
look how young you look.

02:44.101 --> 02:45.771
I sympathize with y'all.

02:45.839 --> 02:50.245
Donna makes me listen to Gayle
King on XM Radio 19 hours a day.

02:50.313 --> 02:51.882
I tried to kill myself by

02:51.950 --> 02:54.485
swallowing a nail clipper,
but I passed it.

02:54.553 --> 02:55.955
What the hell
happened to us?

02:56.022 --> 02:58.091
We used to be able to do
whatever the hell we wanted.

02:58.160 --> 02:59.760
Now here we are,
in the prime of our lives,

02:59.828 --> 03:01.513
and we're slaves to our women.

03:01.582 --> 03:03.450
I know. An exciting
day for me

03:03.518 --> 03:05.321
is when I watch
wheelchair porn.

03:05.389 --> 03:06.989
Boy, do the sparks
fly on those.

03:07.057 --> 03:08.492
Oh, is it hot?

03:08.560 --> 03:11.647
Nah, it's mostly just chairs
smashing into each other.

03:11.715 --> 03:13.950
Sometimes the director
has to come on camera

03:14.019 --> 03:15.454
just to turn the
chairs around.

03:15.521 --> 03:17.307
Well, why don't we make
our own excitement?

03:17.374 --> 03:19.010
- What do you mean?
- I don't know, like,

03:19.078 --> 03:20.145
maybe the four
of us should

03:20.214 --> 03:21.347
do something
to reclaim our freedom.

03:21.432 --> 03:22.983
Like go on a road trip,
find some adventure.

03:23.051 --> 03:24.586
Quagmire,
that's a great idea!

03:24.653 --> 03:26.105
Let's do a road trip!
Who's in?

03:28.794 --> 03:29.961
No. No, no.

03:30.028 --> 03:31.531
No, n-not you, Seamus.

03:31.599 --> 03:32.601
SEAMUS:
Ah, poo.

03:35.939 --> 03:37.875
All right, listen up, ladies.

03:37.943 --> 03:40.512
We got something to say and we
ain't taking "no" for an answer.

03:40.580 --> 03:41.948
We are going on a road trip.

03:42.016 --> 03:43.466
We don't know how long
we'll be gone,

03:43.534 --> 03:45.337
and don't expect a call
from us to check in.

03:45.405 --> 03:47.574
This trip is about men
being men.

03:47.642 --> 03:49.644
We will drive
after a couple of beers

03:49.712 --> 03:51.431
and not make a big
federal case about it.

03:51.499 --> 03:53.769
We're gonna sneeze and not
put our hand over (bleep).

03:53.837 --> 03:55.739
And there ain't nothing
you can do to stop us!

03:55.806 --> 03:56.873
Yeah, okay with me.

03:56.941 --> 03:57.775
- Sure.
- Fine.

03:57.843 --> 03:59.211
That'll be nice.

03:59.279 --> 04:00.747
It'll give us a chance
to have some girl time.

04:00.814 --> 04:02.884
Oh. All right, then.

04:02.951 --> 04:04.052
Where are you boys going?

04:04.120 --> 04:05.221
We're going to New Orleans.

04:05.289 --> 04:07.090
The party capital of America.

04:07.158 --> 04:09.361
Home of the
All-You-Can-Pee Street.

04:09.429 --> 04:12.198
I'll tell you one thing, it's
all about the beads down there.

04:19.746 --> 04:21.932
We all know
what's going on here.

04:22.000 --> 04:23.836
It's just implied,
but we all know

04:23.903 --> 04:25.422
what's going on
in this thought bubble.

04:25.506 --> 04:27.376
The kids don't know, but we do.

04:41.900 --> 04:45.488
Boy, I'm sure getting my money's
worth out of this rental car.

04:45.572 --> 04:46.958
Okay, all right,
I got one.

04:47.043 --> 04:49.578
Would you rather be a hobo
with a five percent chance

04:49.629 --> 04:51.498
of getting inherited
by a rich guy

04:51.582 --> 04:54.671
or be Hitler two years before
the end of World War II?

04:54.755 --> 04:56.589
'Cause you know you're gonna
have to shoot yourself,

04:56.640 --> 04:58.310
but you still got two
more years as Hitler.

04:58.394 --> 05:00.096
If you're the hobo, do you, uh,

05:00.147 --> 05:02.467
have a place to sleep,
like an underpass or...?

05:02.518 --> 05:03.468
Different every night.

05:03.519 --> 05:05.154
As Hitler, can I change

05:05.238 --> 05:07.141
certain policies
so that maybe I'm looked on

05:07.192 --> 05:09.027
more favorably
at the end of the war?

05:09.112 --> 05:11.415
No, you already screwed up
big-time-- lot of dead Jews.

05:11.483 --> 05:14.169
Am I a blue state
or a red state hobo?

05:14.254 --> 05:16.656
Blue, but
Midwestern blue.

05:16.709 --> 05:18.210
Oh, boy.
(grumbling)

05:18.295 --> 05:20.263
I don't think so,
it's cold out there.

05:20.331 --> 05:21.665
Am I allowed
to alter the mustache?

05:21.717 --> 05:23.685
Dude, why do you keep
trying to make Hitler work?

05:23.770 --> 05:27.008
Am I allowed to kill other hobos
to increase my odds?

05:27.059 --> 05:28.527
Kill anyone you
like; you're a hobo.

05:28.611 --> 05:30.062
Am I a walking hobo?

05:30.147 --> 05:32.033
No. Quagmire and Cleveland
are, but you're not.

05:32.118 --> 05:34.070
So, wait, I would also
be a paralyzed Hitler?

05:34.155 --> 05:35.322
Yeah.

05:35.373 --> 05:36.958
Would I be
a black Hitler?

05:37.025 --> 05:38.545
Yes. No.

05:38.628 --> 05:40.714
Well, wait a minute,
now how come I got to be

05:40.799 --> 05:42.249
crippled Hitler
and he's still white Hitler?

05:42.334 --> 05:44.420
If you got such a problem with
it, Joe, just be the hobo!

05:44.505 --> 05:45.672
This one isn't very fun.

05:45.723 --> 05:47.509
Wait a minute, where are we?

05:47.560 --> 05:49.980
Yeah, this doesn't look like
the main highway anymore.

05:50.047 --> 05:51.231
You think we made
a wrong turn?

05:51.315 --> 05:52.384
I hope not.

05:52.435 --> 05:54.021
These backwoods parts
of the Deep South

05:54.072 --> 05:55.940
ain't a place
you want to get lost in.

05:56.024 --> 05:57.777
(siren wailing)

05:57.861 --> 05:58.694
Oh, no.

06:02.117 --> 06:03.469
Don't worry
about it, guys.

06:03.537 --> 06:05.506
I read nowhere that Southern
sheriffs really want

06:05.574 --> 06:07.408
to be talked down to by
big-shot Northerners.

06:09.580 --> 06:10.731
Afternoon.

06:10.799 --> 06:12.234
Officer, what is it?

06:12.301 --> 06:14.203
We are in a tremendous
urban rush.

06:14.271 --> 06:16.307
You fellas ain't from
around here, are you?

06:16.375 --> 06:18.143
Hey, Sheriff,
I'm trying to learn Southern.

06:18.211 --> 06:19.513
Is this saying anything?

06:19.580 --> 06:21.783
A-doy-doy-doy-doy!

06:21.851 --> 06:24.388
We're very sorry, Sheriff,
and we want to cooperate

06:24.456 --> 06:26.158
to the fullest extent possible.

06:26.226 --> 06:27.242
You threatening me?

06:27.310 --> 06:28.377
Uh, no, sir.

06:28.445 --> 06:29.980
Who you calling "sir," boy?

06:30.048 --> 06:32.618
I'm an officer of the law,
paid by this county.

06:32.686 --> 06:35.190
And I can't help noticing
you got a headlight out.

06:35.257 --> 06:36.592
Really?
I don't see any...

06:38.162 --> 06:40.598
And I see that turn signal
ain't working neither.

06:41.534 --> 06:42.668
Now, look, sir,

06:42.736 --> 06:44.171
I'm a police officer, too.

06:44.239 --> 06:46.241
I know all the games;
I use them myself.

06:46.308 --> 06:48.495
So what do you say
we just work something out?

06:48.579 --> 06:49.780
So, you're a cop, huh?

06:49.848 --> 06:52.252
Let me see your badge.

06:53.755 --> 06:55.657
Looks like you're
a civilian now.

06:55.725 --> 06:58.428
I'm gonna have to
search your vehicle.

07:00.282 --> 07:01.267
Well, lookie here.

07:01.334 --> 07:02.986
What do we got in this thing?

07:03.054 --> 07:05.040
Oh, come on!
You planted that there!

07:05.108 --> 07:06.208
We had drugs?

07:06.276 --> 07:08.010
Oh, my God,
why am I driving drunk

07:08.062 --> 07:09.363
when I could've been
driving high?

07:09.431 --> 07:11.533
You boys are in
a lot of trouble.

07:11.602 --> 07:13.403
Dispatch,
Sheriff Nichols.

07:13.471 --> 07:14.622
Bringing in four
perpetrators

07:14.690 --> 07:16.358
under suspicion of
drug possession.

07:16.426 --> 07:18.729
Descriptions: one
African-American,

07:18.797 --> 07:20.631
one crippled, one
skinny, one handsome.

07:20.700 --> 07:21.934
Yes.

07:22.002 --> 07:24.004
You're all coming down
to the station with me.

07:24.072 --> 07:25.039
Aw, crap!

07:25.106 --> 07:26.609
Hang on, hang on,
you guys.

07:26.676 --> 07:28.212
Don't worry. I know how to
speak this guy's language.

07:28.263 --> 07:31.317
Keith Urban.

07:31.384 --> 07:32.752
Go on.

07:32.820 --> 07:34.756
Brett Favre.

07:34.824 --> 07:35.791
Uh-huh.

07:35.858 --> 07:37.827
I'm listening.

07:37.895 --> 07:39.564
William H. Macy?

07:39.632 --> 07:41.768
You guys are going
away for a long time.

07:53.469 --> 07:54.368
Look at this, Cleveland.

07:54.369 --> 07:56.120
Front of the bus,
back of the bus,

07:56.171 --> 07:57.958
middle of the bus--
you guys are doing great.

07:58.009 --> 07:59.209
I can't believe this.

07:59.293 --> 08:01.045
Two weeks in prison
on trumped-up charges.

08:01.129 --> 08:02.982
That trial was a total sham.

08:03.050 --> 08:05.420
Yeah, I knew we were in trouble
the minute I saw the jury.

08:07.707 --> 08:09.776
Well, at least they're
a jury of our peers.

08:09.844 --> 08:11.914
I don't think they see it
that way, Peter.

08:18.659 --> 08:20.362
Hello, gentlemen.

08:20.429 --> 08:21.863
I am the warden.

08:21.931 --> 08:24.601
You are here
because you are criminals.

08:24.670 --> 08:26.037
This is not a resort.

08:26.088 --> 08:28.174
You will be worked harder
than you have ever

08:28.225 --> 08:30.895
been worked in your miserable,
pathetic lives.

08:30.979 --> 08:32.915
And play
harder, right?

08:32.983 --> 08:34.084
I bet.

08:34.152 --> 08:35.052
Step forward, maggot!

08:36.740 --> 08:38.223
(grunts)

08:38.275 --> 08:40.411
Next time, that'll be you.

08:40.479 --> 08:42.381
Well, why wasn't
it him this time?!

08:42.449 --> 08:44.418
Oh, I'm so scared.

08:44.503 --> 08:45.587
(grunting)

08:45.672 --> 08:47.122
Peter, stop it!

08:47.206 --> 08:49.560
Yeah, you're real big when
you got that stick, ain't you?

08:49.627 --> 08:50.795
Okay, I'll stop now.

08:54.235 --> 08:56.104
This is so much fun,
isn't it?

08:56.172 --> 08:57.139
I know.

08:57.207 --> 08:58.541
What should we talk
about next?

08:58.609 --> 09:00.479
I know, let's talk
about actresses.

09:00.545 --> 09:01.647
Ooh, yeah.

09:01.715 --> 09:03.651
I feel like Natalie Portman

09:03.719 --> 09:06.155
thinks she's so much better
than everybody.

09:06.223 --> 09:08.492
She's nothing, and her
husband's a nobody.

09:08.560 --> 09:09.894
Why does Laura
Linney always

09:09.962 --> 09:11.280
look like she's just
finished skiing?

09:11.347 --> 09:12.683
I don't know
who that is.

09:12.751 --> 09:14.986
<i>Really? The Big C?
Love Actually?</i>

09:15.054 --> 09:16.289
No, never heard of her.

09:16.356 --> 09:17.591
Would you know
who she was

09:17.659 --> 09:19.326
if I said Tyler
Perry's Laura Linney?

09:19.394 --> 09:20.695
Ooh, I love her.

09:26.239 --> 09:28.358
Oh, God, it's so hot out here.

09:28.427 --> 09:30.445
Yeah, you knew it was
gonna be hot when you heard

09:30.513 --> 09:32.782
that lonesome slide guitar
and that hawk's cry.

09:32.850 --> 09:35.320
(guitar plays somber riff)

09:35.387 --> 09:37.290
(hawk screeches)

09:37.358 --> 09:38.860
Hey! This ain't break time!

09:38.927 --> 09:41.547
Get back to work!

09:41.614 --> 09:43.984
♪ Gonna see Miss Liza ♪

09:44.052 --> 09:46.338
♪ Gonna go to Mississippi ♪

09:46.390 --> 09:48.909
♪ Gonna see Miss Liza ♪

09:48.977 --> 09:51.180
♪ Gonna go to Mississippi ♪

09:51.231 --> 09:53.683
♪ Gonna see Miss Liza ♪

09:53.735 --> 09:55.403
♪ Gonna go to Mississippi. ♪

09:55.487 --> 09:57.373
Man, listen to
what the black guys are doing.

09:57.458 --> 09:59.193
We need a white
guy work song.

09:59.261 --> 10:00.664
(lively music playing)

10:00.715 --> 10:01.664
♪ Hello ♪

10:01.715 --> 10:02.632
♪ How are you? ♪

10:02.699 --> 10:03.635
♪ How's the folks? ♪

10:03.702 --> 10:05.019
♪ What's new? ♪

10:05.087 --> 10:06.172
♪ I'm great ♪
♪ That's good ♪

10:06.223 --> 10:07.140
♪ Ha-ha ♪

10:07.208 --> 10:08.476
♪ Knock wood ♪

10:08.543 --> 10:09.761
♪ Well, well ♪
♪ That's life ♪

10:09.846 --> 10:10.814
♪ What do you know? ♪

10:10.881 --> 10:12.066
♪ How's the wife? ♪

10:12.150 --> 10:13.434
♪ Got to run ♪
♪ Oh, my ♪

10:13.502 --> 10:14.437
♪ Ta-ta ♪
♪ Olive oil ♪

10:14.505 --> 10:15.521
♪ Good-bye. ♪

10:15.572 --> 10:17.424
(shoes tapping rhythmically)

10:26.675 --> 10:28.109
You Peter Griffin?

10:28.177 --> 10:29.845
Oh, yeah, thanks.

10:29.912 --> 10:31.264
What the hell is that?

10:31.331 --> 10:32.534
It's a jet pack.

10:32.600 --> 10:34.519
I'll come back for you guys,
I promise.

10:38.260 --> 10:41.665
You're my friend and everything
and I feel bad saying this,

10:41.733 --> 10:43.868
but I wanted to see you fail.

10:54.087 --> 10:56.322
Official prediction:
when they let us out of here,

10:56.390 --> 10:58.560
we're gonna have to go through
the prison gift shop.

10:58.628 --> 11:00.430
(men grumbling)
Oh, I hate doing that.

11:00.498 --> 11:01.999
That's how
they get you.

11:02.066 --> 11:04.471
Man, it's gonna feel so good
to walk out of here tomorrow.

11:04.537 --> 11:06.706
Yeah, you know,
the time actually went by faster

11:06.775 --> 11:07.910
than I would have thought.

11:07.977 --> 11:09.646
Uh, you know something?

11:09.713 --> 11:11.349
We left Quahog to find adventure

11:11.417 --> 11:13.853
and get away from all
those lame chores at home,

11:13.921 --> 11:15.488
but I'll tell you this.

11:15.555 --> 11:18.726
Looking back on it now, I don't
think our lives are so bad.

11:18.795 --> 11:20.630
Yeah, I sure do miss Lois
and the kids.

11:20.698 --> 11:21.966
I'll tell you one thing.

11:22.034 --> 11:24.002
When I get home,
I'm gonna sleep like a log.

11:24.070 --> 11:27.024
Hey, I'm gonna plug in the
night-light if you don't mind.

11:27.092 --> 11:28.443
Actually, you know what?

11:28.510 --> 11:31.047
I'm gonna go ahead and
ask you to not do that.

11:31.114 --> 11:33.669
Knock off that chitchat!
It's lights out!

11:33.737 --> 11:35.972
Oh, hey, Warden, since
it's our last night in here,

11:36.040 --> 11:37.809
can I have a glass of milk?

11:37.877 --> 11:39.279
I feel like having
dream diarrhea.

11:39.346 --> 11:40.964
Last night?

11:41.032 --> 11:42.701
Where do you think
y'all are going?

11:42.768 --> 11:45.839
Says here you got another
30 days on your sentence.

11:45.907 --> 11:48.477
What?! But the court said we're
supposed to go home tomorrow!

11:48.546 --> 11:50.547
Well, the court
ain't here, is it?

11:50.614 --> 11:53.368
(Warden laughs)

11:53.436 --> 11:54.838
Oh, man, how the hell
are we gonna do this

11:54.906 --> 11:56.006
for another 30 days?

11:56.074 --> 11:57.243
(man chuckles)

11:57.311 --> 11:59.412
That's the way
it goes around here.

11:59.479 --> 12:02.083
Once you come in,
you're never allowed to leave.

12:02.152 --> 12:04.754
I got my sentence extended
30 days once.

12:04.822 --> 12:07.159
That was 45 years ago.

12:07.226 --> 12:08.578
Oh, my God,
you hear that?

12:08.645 --> 12:10.079
We're gonna be stuck
in here forever!

12:10.147 --> 12:11.799
Oh, God, what are we gonna do?

12:11.866 --> 12:13.303
Well, I know
what I'm gonna do.

12:13.371 --> 12:15.005
If we're gonna be here a while,

12:15.073 --> 12:17.843
I'm gonna find the biggest guy
here and kick his ass.

12:17.911 --> 12:19.044
Wait a minute.
That's me!

12:19.112 --> 12:21.198
Oh, no, I have a knife!

12:28.353 --> 12:29.825
Oh, what are we gonna do?!

12:29.826 --> 12:32.029
They're gonna keep us
locked up here forever!

12:32.080 --> 12:33.849
We're not staying
in here forever.

12:33.917 --> 12:35.484
- We're getting out of here.
- How?

12:35.552 --> 12:37.037
We're breaking out.

12:37.105 --> 12:37.838
What?

12:37.906 --> 12:39.224
Look, sometimes in life,

12:39.292 --> 12:41.578
you got to say, "What the hell,"
and just go for it.

12:41.646 --> 12:43.482
I mean, that's how
we won the Revolutionary War.

12:43.550 --> 12:47.088
Colonel, the British are too
entrenched across the river.

12:47.155 --> 12:48.890
I've told the men
we'll hold our position.

12:52.814 --> 12:54.784
Negative. Tell the men,
we're going across.

12:54.851 --> 12:56.420
But Colonel Goatbanger,
we've...

12:56.487 --> 12:57.972
No, we need to do this,

12:58.040 --> 12:59.708
'cause... for...
'cause of... for strategy.

13:05.487 --> 13:07.421
All right, if we're
gonna break out of here,

13:07.472 --> 13:08.857
we got to get past
these guards.

13:08.924 --> 13:10.327
Well, I got an idea.

13:10.395 --> 13:12.312
It won't be pretty,
but bear with me.

13:12.398 --> 13:13.848
(groaning)

13:13.916 --> 13:15.885
Oh, no, I fell out
of my wheelchair!

13:15.953 --> 13:17.155
(groaning)

13:17.240 --> 13:18.473
(strained groaning, sighs)

13:18.541 --> 13:19.742
Don't help me!

13:19.810 --> 13:21.680
I need to do this on my own!

13:21.747 --> 13:23.715
What are you doing, Joe?
You're embarrassing us.

13:23.784 --> 13:25.117
Oh, really?
Are they looking?

13:28.223 --> 13:30.961
No. They're actually going
to great lengths to avoid it.

13:31.029 --> 13:32.596
Exactly. No one wants

13:32.665 --> 13:34.934
to watch a handicap
struggle for independence.

13:35.002 --> 13:38.040
This will buy us at least
15 minutes of averted gazes.

13:38.108 --> 13:40.077
All right,
I'm gonna nail this home.

13:40.145 --> 13:41.979
Oh! Oh, this is
so humiliating.

13:42.032 --> 13:45.769
I'm about to be an
adult man crying.

13:45.836 --> 13:47.673
(Joe sobs loudly)

13:55.186 --> 13:57.221
I can't walk!

13:57.289 --> 13:59.325
Why the hell
can't I walk?!

13:59.393 --> 14:02.263
This isn't
part of the act anymore!

14:02.347 --> 14:04.250
No, no, no, no,
don't look.

14:04.318 --> 14:06.454
If you make eye contact,
you'll have to help.

14:08.492 --> 14:10.227
Hey, they're
getting away!

14:11.530 --> 14:13.282
Release the dogs!

14:13.366 --> 14:15.453
(barking)

14:16.739 --> 14:18.842
(high-pitched barking)

14:20.762 --> 14:22.515
(barking continues,
chains jangling)

14:36.605 --> 14:37.873
(barking)

14:45.955 --> 14:47.122
Oh, we did it!

14:47.174 --> 14:48.425
Your plan worked, Joe!

14:48.476 --> 14:50.344
I told you those guards
would turn away.

14:50.428 --> 14:51.813
Yeah, Joe, that
was amazing!

14:51.897 --> 14:54.251
That was easier than taking
candy from a premature baby.

14:54.318 --> 14:56.155
(rhythmic beeping)

14:58.492 --> 15:01.513
I'm, uh...
I'm just gonna take this.

15:08.074 --> 15:09.944
(loud laughter)

15:11.631 --> 15:13.684
Hey, I got an idea

15:13.752 --> 15:16.054
for something that's gonna
be so (bleep) funny.

15:16.122 --> 15:18.559
(whispering)

15:18.626 --> 15:19.827
Okay, Bonnie,
go get it.

15:19.894 --> 15:21.462
It's in the closet.

15:21.530 --> 15:24.485
Brian! Brian,
come out here!

15:24.553 --> 15:26.104
What are you doing?!

15:26.172 --> 15:27.323
I'm reading.

15:27.391 --> 15:29.661
What... what... what...

15:29.729 --> 15:31.496
What are you reading?

15:31.564 --> 15:33.667
Well, I was just finishing
Jonathan Franzen's book.

15:33.734 --> 15:35.670
You know, I'll admit
it has its moments,

15:35.738 --> 15:37.173
but it's completely
overrated.

15:37.241 --> 15:39.911
I mean, I'm not saying I
wrote something similar to it

15:39.978 --> 15:41.580
several years ago,
but I am saying...

15:41.649 --> 15:42.949
Grab him!
(laughter)

15:43.017 --> 15:45.286
What? What? What? What?
Hey, what are you doing?! Hey!

15:45.355 --> 15:47.106
- Get his paw! Hold still!
- Hey! Hey! Hey! What?

15:47.190 --> 15:48.775
- Push him down onto all fours!
- No. What are you do...?

15:48.843 --> 15:50.346
- I don't want to do this.
- If he really starts freaking out,

15:50.413 --> 15:51.614
put your pinkie in his butt!
- Aah!

15:51.681 --> 15:52.783
(laughter,
Brian groaning)

15:52.851 --> 15:54.803
Calm down!
Calm down!

15:54.871 --> 15:56.088
(grunting)

15:56.155 --> 15:58.508
(laughter)

15:58.576 --> 16:00.078
Now Stewie!

16:00.146 --> 16:02.883
All right, I guess
this is the night bitches die.

16:05.438 --> 16:07.724
I wonder what the
chain gang did today.

16:07.775 --> 16:09.644
I hope we're not
missing anything cool.

16:09.728 --> 16:11.263
Maybe we should go back.

16:11.331 --> 16:12.482
Hey, guys, look,
there's a house.

16:14.053 --> 16:15.471
Maybe there's something inside

16:15.539 --> 16:17.256
we can use
to get these chains off.

16:25.838 --> 16:28.092
It looks like
nobody's home.

16:28.143 --> 16:30.179
Hey, these look like
handcuff and shackle keys.

16:30.247 --> 16:31.181
How do you know that?

16:31.249 --> 16:32.549
(chuckles)

16:32.617 --> 16:34.519
These are handcuff
and shackle keys.

16:34.603 --> 16:36.456
Hey, it worked!

16:38.410 --> 16:40.380
You know, there's an awful lot
of pictures

16:40.447 --> 16:41.948
of the sheriff in this house.

16:42.016 --> 16:43.317
Well, he's a good-looking man.

16:43.385 --> 16:46.056
I'll bet a lot of people
in town have pictures of him.

16:47.241 --> 16:49.695
Oh, no! It's the sheriff!

16:49.763 --> 16:51.097
Quick, into the closet!

16:58.528 --> 17:00.262
(farting)
Who's there?

17:00.330 --> 17:01.898
PETER (in high-pitched voice):
Just me, sweetie.

17:01.966 --> 17:03.602
Oh, I didn't know
you were home.

17:03.670 --> 17:05.472
What are you doing
in the closet there?

17:05.539 --> 17:06.940
Um... wife things?

17:07.008 --> 17:09.543
Oh, all right. Well, I'll only
be home for a minute.

17:09.612 --> 17:11.247
Some prisoners escaped
from the work camp,

17:11.315 --> 17:13.283
and I'm helping the warden
track 'em down.

17:13.352 --> 17:15.856
Oh. Well, maybe you
should let 'em go.

17:15.923 --> 17:17.575
You know I can't do that.

17:17.643 --> 17:19.311
You're always working.

17:19.379 --> 17:21.215
I wish you'd spend
more time at home.

17:21.283 --> 17:22.550
More time with me.

17:22.617 --> 17:23.785
Maybe you're right, honey.

17:23.853 --> 17:25.254
Maybe I do work too much.

17:25.321 --> 17:26.590
You know what?

17:26.658 --> 17:28.427
I'm gonna let
those fugitives go.

17:28.495 --> 17:29.829
You'd do that for me?

17:29.896 --> 17:31.548
I'd do anything for you.

17:31.616 --> 17:32.950
I love you.

17:33.018 --> 17:34.453
I love you, too!

17:34.521 --> 17:36.523
Now, come out here
and give me a kiss!

17:36.607 --> 17:38.226
Peter, no!

17:38.294 --> 17:40.196
Wait minute!
I don't have a wife!

17:40.264 --> 17:43.168
(gunshots)

17:43.235 --> 17:45.521
(gunfire continues)

17:45.589 --> 17:46.808
(sirens wailing)

17:46.892 --> 17:48.559
(tires squealing)

17:54.705 --> 17:57.241
(train whistle blowing)

17:57.292 --> 17:58.610
Head for the tracks!

18:01.466 --> 18:02.550
(gunfire)

18:02.617 --> 18:04.787
Oh, no!
They're shooting at us!

18:04.839 --> 18:06.892
Good thing bad guys are
such terrible shots.

18:06.959 --> 18:09.579
Man, these guys are elusive!

18:09.646 --> 18:11.098
Quick!
Hop on!

18:18.144 --> 18:20.530
- All right, we did it.
- We made it.

18:20.615 --> 18:22.366
That was a
close one!

18:22.450 --> 18:23.952
(sighs)
Well, guys, we made it.

18:24.004 --> 18:26.456
Boy, I feel like
I haven't eaten in a week.

18:26.509 --> 18:27.960
Hey, if we pass
a McDaniel's

18:28.011 --> 18:29.796
or a Burger Queen,
let's hop out.

18:29.847 --> 18:31.549
Oh, that's right,
we're on television.

18:31.633 --> 18:33.501
Oh, I'd love a
flame-broiled Bopper!

18:33.553 --> 18:36.808
So frustrating. We all know
what we're talking about.

18:36.859 --> 18:38.643
(train chugging,
train whistle blowing quietly)

18:41.516 --> 18:45.188
Well, this was
quite an adventure.

18:45.239 --> 18:47.626
Yeah, it's good to be
back in familiar territory.

18:47.693 --> 18:49.913
(gun chambers cocking)

18:49.980 --> 18:51.466
Where do y'all think
you're going?

18:51.534 --> 18:53.586
You boys are fugitives
of my county,

18:53.670 --> 18:55.722
and I'm gonna take you back.

18:55.790 --> 18:56.908
Oh, no!

18:56.976 --> 18:58.194
I don't think so.

18:58.261 --> 19:01.131
You're in my jurisdiction now,
Sheriff Butt Breath.

19:06.141 --> 19:08.193
Wow, Joe,
how'd you pull that off?

19:08.261 --> 19:10.497
I put in a call from
the McDaniel's pay phone

19:10.565 --> 19:13.068
while you guys were getting that
nine-piece chicken McFingers

19:13.137 --> 19:15.773
and those Diet Conks
and those Fresh Fries.

19:15.841 --> 19:18.244
Oh, come on. They-They
don't own "French fries!"

19:18.295 --> 19:21.349
You know, you got some nerve
driving around my town

19:21.417 --> 19:24.153
with a busted headlight.

19:24.221 --> 19:27.526
And a busted windshield.

19:27.593 --> 19:29.947
And an untreated flesh wound.

19:30.015 --> 19:32.402
(groaning)

19:32.469 --> 19:35.155
You took an oath just
the same as me, Sheriff.

19:35.223 --> 19:36.625
To protect and serve.

19:36.692 --> 19:38.395
Not to harass and douche.

19:38.479 --> 19:40.147
Just 'cause you have
a badge doesn't mean

19:40.214 --> 19:42.066
you can treat people
any way you like.

19:42.152 --> 19:43.987
And as a law enforcement
professional,

19:44.054 --> 19:46.108
you have an obligation to be
more ethically upstanding

19:46.192 --> 19:49.445
than the average man, not less.

19:49.530 --> 19:52.219
Now, get the hell
out of my town.

20:00.332 --> 20:02.335
Nice going, Joe!

20:02.403 --> 20:04.506
Well, it's great
being back in the North

20:04.573 --> 20:05.975
where people
are civilized.

20:06.043 --> 20:08.962
Hey, what, are you guys
all on a date?

20:09.030 --> 20:11.000
Gay!

20:14.406 --> 20:16.608
Oh, my God, Peter,
what an experience.

20:16.676 --> 20:19.547
But the important thing is
you're home safe.

20:19.615 --> 20:22.451
Yeah. And you know, I guess I
learned something from all this.

20:22.519 --> 20:23.888
(sighs)
You know what?

20:23.956 --> 20:25.741
We've done this a billion
times, so you know what?

20:25.809 --> 20:28.479
I'm just gonna
do the cadences.

20:28.547 --> 20:30.381
(speaking gibberish)

20:31.919 --> 20:33.771
(speaking gibberish)

20:35.442 --> 20:37.276
(speaking gibberish)

20:39.481 --> 20:40.933
(speaking gibberish)

20:41.000 --> 20:44.539
(speaking
gibberish)

20:44.540 --> 21:45.640
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru